 =\\frac{k}{10}x-\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line $kx-10y=3$ is $\\frac{k}{10}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n2\\cdot (\\frac{k}{10})=-1\\,⟹\\,k=-5.\n$$" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243862 13194139533646 true] [17592186243861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533646 true] [17592186243861 1041 "field-1" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243862 13194139533646 true] [17592186243861 1110 #uuid "3fe24769-facb-561b-8907-799770c5d13a" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243862 1034 "-5" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533646 true] [17592186243862 1111 #uuid "5d252f6a-a6ed-5b6f-839d-8757f218ea91" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243864 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1089 "q-215941" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1100 "The lines $y=-5x+3$ and $3kx-5y=9$ are perpendicular. What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1113 #uuid "dedc61d6-f231-5dad-bf68-62d6505aac80" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1138 false 13194139533646 true] [17592186243863 1145 "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\n- The first line is in slope-intercept form, and the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So the slope of the line $y=-5x+3$ is $-5.$\n\n- To find the slope of $3kx-5y=9,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx-5y & =9 \\\\ 5y & =3kx-9 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3k}{5}x-\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line $3kx-5y=9$ is $\\frac{3k}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-5)\\cdot (\\frac{3k}{5})=-1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" 13194139533646 true] [17592186243864 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243865 13194139533646 true] [17592186243864 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533646 true] [17592186243864 1041 "field-1